&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Electra&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Air travel is about to become something more: more direct, more accessible, and more connected to the places where people live, work and want to be. Every day in the U.S., people make 35 million trips of 50–500 miles, stuck in traffic or routed through crowded hubs. Chances are, you&#39;ve been one of them. At Electra, we&#39;re changing that with the EL9, a nine-passenger, hybrid-electric aircraft that takes off and lands in just 150 feet. Our Ultra Short technology opens up thousands of new places to fly, beyond conventional runways, congested airports and long drives. We&#39;re backed by Lockheed Martin, Honeywell and Safran. Operators worldwide have signed intent-to-purchase agreements for the first 2,200 aircraft we produce, and we&#39;re moving toward first test flights in 2027.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Getting a new kind of aircraft airborne takes more than ambition. It takes our kind of bold: people who think big while working in the real world. Who move ideas into action and collaborate without silos. Who put people first and make room at the table for everyone. Who challenge one another without diminishing one another.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Sound like you? Then look beyond what you thought were your own limits, and help us take flight beyond runways.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Electra&#39;s Senior Structural Assembly Manufacturing Engineer, you&#39;ll play a key role in developing and industrializing the structural assembly processes for the EL9 aircraft, working from early product development through prototype build, production implementation, and ramp-up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work closely with Product Engineering during aircraft development to ensure structural designs incorporate Design for Manufacturing and Assembly (DFMA) principles and can be efficiently, repeatably, and reliably produced. You&#39;ll bring a hands-on manufacturing perspective to structural design decisions, evaluating assembly sequence, tolerance management, access, tooling, fastening and joining methods, inspection requirements, producibility, and production risk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the EL9 transitions from design into physical hardware, you&#39;ll help translate released engineering into executable manufacturing processes and support prototype and initial aircraft builds. You&#39;ll work closely with airframe manufacturing suppliers, providing on-site Manufacturing Engineering oversight and liaison support as needed to ensure proper information flow, resolve technical and quality issues, support the incorporation of product changes and support supply chain on contract management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to influence both how the aircraft is designed and how it is ultimately built, while helping establish Electra&#39;s structural assembly manufacturing supply chain capability from the ground up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Engineering throughout aircraft development to ensure structural designs incorporate Design for Manufacturing and Assembly (DFMA) principles and support efficient, repeatable, and scalable production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review aircraft structural designs, assemblies, drawings, models, and engineering changes from a manufacturing perspective, providing recommendations related to producibility, assembly sequence, access, tolerance stack-up, fastening and joining methods, tooling, inspection, and production risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in design trade studies, concept reviews, and design reviews, representing Manufacturing Engineering and identifying manufacturing constraints and opportunities early in the development cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide Manufacturing Engineering oversight and liaison support at airframe and structural suppliers, working directly with supplier manufacturing teams to clarify design and manufacturing intent, resolve producibility and assembly issues, and maintain program execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the airframe supplier Tooling Engineering to define assembly tooling concepts, requirements, locating strategies, interfaces, and implementation plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review supplier manufacturing approaches, build plans, assembly processes, tooling concepts, and production readiness to ensure alignment with Electra&#39;s engineering requirements and program objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support prototype fabrication, development aircraft assembly, first builds, and production implementation, providing hands-on Manufacturing Engineering support to resolve issues encountered during structural assembly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate technical resolution of manufacturing issues and nonconformances with Product Engineering, Stress, Quality, Supplier Quality, Supply Chain, and other stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capture manufacturing lessons learned and supplier feedback from prototype and initial production builds and drive those learnings back into product design, manufacturing processes, tooling, and planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support structural assembly production ramp-up by identifying constraints, resolving manufacturing issues, improving assembly processes, and driving improvements in quality, cost, schedule, and production rate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the development and continuous improvement of Electra manufacturing engineering standards, methods, processes, and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Mechanical, Aerospace, Aeronautical, Manufacturing Engineering, or a related engineering field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of aerospace manufacturing engineering experience, with significant experience in aircraft structural assembly and industrialization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on knowledge of aircraft structural assembly processes, including metallic and/or composite airframe structures, drilling, fastening, joining, shimming, sealing, alignment, and major structural integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience applying Design for Manufacturing and Assembly (DFMA) principles during aircraft product development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reviewing engineering drawings, 3D models, GD&amp;amp;T, tolerances, and engineering changes from a manufacturing and assembly perspective.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing manufacturing plans, assembly sequences, work instructions, tooling requirements, and manufacturing engineering documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting prototype, development, or first-production aircraft builds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with aircraft structures suppliers or manufacturing partners and supporting production activities in a factory environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work effectively across Product Engineering, Stress, Quality, Supplier Quality, Supply Chain, Tooling, and Production organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills and ability to make sound engineering recommendations in a fast-moving aircraft development environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to work effectively across internal teams and external suppliers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability and willingness to travel to supplier and manufacturing locations as required by program needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with clean-sheet aircraft development and transition from prototype into production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with major structural assemblies such as fuselage, wing, empennage, control surfaces, or other primary airframe structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with aircraft assembly tooling, jigs, fixtures, determinant assembly, or advanced assembly methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with digital manufacturing tools, PLM/MES environments, manufacturing BOMs, and 3D model-based manufacturing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with supplier industrialization, production readiness assessments, or manufacturing capability reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with MRB, root cause corrective action, and production nonconformance resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AS9100 aerospace quality management systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;This range reflects the anticipated hiring range across all eligible locations; actual compensation is determined based on your relevant experience, skills, and geographic location. Total compensation includes performance bonus and comprehensive benefits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Compensation Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$130,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$155,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Medical, dental, and vision insurance; STD, LTD, and life insurance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Generous PTO, sick leave, and company holidays&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Paid winter break&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;401(k) with immediate vesting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Free catered lunches, coffee, snacks, and drinks at our Manassas headquarters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Free on-site parking&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Electra is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. This position may be subject to ITAR requirements.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About IonQ:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2F&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=IonQ%2C+Inc&amp;amp;index=7&amp;amp;md5=0818ffbedc6dbad8c4d1611ac94c2a0f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;IonQ, Inc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;. [NYSE: IONQ] is the world’s leading quantum platform and merchant supplier - delivering integrated quantum solutions across computing, networking, sensing, and security. IonQ’s newest generation of quantum computers, the IonQ Tempo, is the latest in a line of cutting-edge systems that have been helping customers and partners including &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=Amazon+Web+Services%2C&amp;amp;index=8&amp;amp;md5=a7f94ee9b71a392dca3cd6c413722e51&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Amazon Web Services, &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=and&amp;amp;index=9&amp;amp;md5=2bed627b388878763f41ffe0e4edb16c&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;and &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=AstraZeneca&amp;amp;index=10&amp;amp;md5=757c1f2c2ec94cf3982700106122164f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;AstraZeneca&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt; achieve 20x performance results and accelerate innovation in drug discovery, materials science, financial modeling, logistics, cybersecurity, and defense. In 2025, the company achieved 99.99% two-qubit gate fidelity, &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-achieves-landmark-result-setting-new-world-record-in-quantum-computing&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=setting+a+world+record+in+quantum+computing+performance&amp;amp;index=11&amp;amp;md5=32e9cb88afbd439026a352666cc72c91&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;setting a world record in quantum computing performance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Headquartered in College Park, Maryland, IonQ has operations in California, Colorado, Massachusetts, Tennessee, Washington, Italy, South Korea, Sweden, Switzerland, Canada, and the United Kingdom. Our quantum computing services are available through all major cloud providers, while we also meet the needs of networking and sensing customers across land, sea, air, and space. IonQ is making quantum platforms more accessible and impactful than ever before. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Manufacturing Site (Geneva), Hybrid&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&lt;/strong&gt; 40% domestic and international.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Job ID:&lt;/strong&gt; 1921&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Multi-Site Supply Chain Manager and MRP/ERP Specialist to join our IonQ Quantum Networking &amp;amp; Security Operations Team. As a Supply Chain Manager, you will be part of a cross-functional international team whose mission is to lead IonQ on its journey to build the world’s best quantum computers to solve the world’s most complex problems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will be responsible for ensuring reliable production planning and material availability across all division products and programs including Quantum Networking &amp;amp; Security projects while managing and optimizing ERP/MRP processes across multiple manufacturing sites. Working as a core member of the division production leadership team, you will lead a team of planner and warehouse specialists driving standardization and best practices. You will collaborate closely with Manufacturing Managers, Sales, Procurement, and Finance. The ideal candidate is process-minded, structured problem-solver with a bias for action, and strong cross-functional communicator in an international multi-site environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SIOP &amp;amp; Supply Planning&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Receive the sales forecast from the Sales/Commercial team across all division and validate it for completeness, consistency, and feasibility before use in planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate customer demand and validated forecasts into capacity, and material plans across the sites ensuring alignment between Manufacturing, Procurement and Finance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the demand and supply review identifying gaps between demand material availability, and inventory targets, and developing mitigation scenarios and recommendations for the Senior Operations Director.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate closely with the Procurement function on material availability, supplier lead times, supply risks, and constraints, ensuring that key risks and potential shortages are identified early and incorporated into SIOP scenarios.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and optimize inventory targets and policies in line with SIOP objectives, balancing customer service and revenue requirements with working capital, excess inventory, and obsolescence risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and monitor key SIOP and Supply Chain KPIs: On Time Delivery (OTD), capacity utilization, inventory turns, and lead times.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Team Leadership&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a distributed team of demand planning and warehouse/stock specialists, setting clear goals while fostering a culture of data-driven decision-making and continuous improvement (Lean/Six Sigma mindset).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish common ways of working, tools, and standards across sites to unify the supply chain function at division level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MRP / ERP Management&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as subject matter expert for the MRP/ERP system regarding demand planning capabilities, and drive improvements to configuration, workflows, and data quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with IT/business systems teams on ERP upgrades, patches, and enhancements affecting planning modules across all sites; lead UAT (user acceptance testing) for planning-related system changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Finance Reporting&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and deliver a monthly production and delivery forecast to Finance to support anticipation of next month&#39;s revenues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Finance on monthly sales forecasts (revenue and volume implications), budget and variance analysis (actual vs. forecast/budget) at division level.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and coordinate the annual physical inventory count at each site ensuring accuracy and working with Finance to reconcile results against ERP records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s degree in industrial engineering, Supply Chain Management, or related field required;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of progressive supply chain experience focused on demand/supply planning in a manufacturing environment. Experience in the electronics industry preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating across multiple sites and ability to standardize processes and drive alignment across locations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in leading a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and statistical data handling skills; advanced Excel required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep, hands-on expertise in MRP/ERP systems (SAP, Oracle, Microsoft Dynamics) is required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Solid knowledge of finance/costing concepts (standard costing, inventory valuation, working capital, etc)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in French and English (written and spoken) required, given the international, cross-functional nature of the role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured problem-solving and data-driven decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross functional influence and clear communication to Senior Leadership and Finance Stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Compensation will vary based on individual factors such as education, qualifications, and experience of the final candidate(s), specific office location, and calibration against relevant market data and internal team equity. Posted base salary figures are subject to change as new market data becomes available. Our benefits include comprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans, matching 401(k), unlimited PTO and paid holidays, parental/adoption leave, legal insurance, and a home technology stipend. Details of participation in these benefit plans will be provided when a candidate receives an offer of employment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At IonQ, we believe in fair treatment, access, opportunity, and advancement for all while striving to identify and eliminate barriers. We empower employees to thrive by fostering a culture of autonomy, productivity, and respect. We are dedicated to creating an environment where individuals can feel welcomed, respected, supported, and valued.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;We are committed to equity and justice. We welcome different voices and viewpoints and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, ancestry, physical and/or mental disability, medical condition, genetic information, marital status, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, age, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. We are proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;The position you are applying for will require access to technology that is subject to U.S. export control and government contract restrictions.&amp;nbsp; Employment with IonQ is contingent on either verifying “U.S. Person” (e.g., U.S. citizen, U.S. national, U.S. permanent resident, or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum) status for export controls and government contracts work, obtaining any necessary license, and/or confirming the availability of a license exception under U.S. export controls.&amp;nbsp; Please note that in the absence of confirming you are a U.S. Person for export control and government contracts work purposes, IonQ may choose not to apply for a license or decline to use a license exception (if available) for you to access export-controlled technology that may require authorization, and similarly, you may not qualify for government contracts work that requires U.S. Persons, and IonQ may decline to proceed with your application on those bases alone.&amp;nbsp; Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Non-Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Due to applicable export control laws and regulations, candidates must be a U.S. citizen or national, U.S. permanent resident (i.e., current Green Card holder), or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum. Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are interested in being a part of our team and mission, we encourage you to apply!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Now is an amazing time to join Nozomi Networks as we build the future of OT and IoT cybersecurity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We defend some of the world’s largest organizations and critical infrastructure in more than 68 countries and we’re just getting started. Our AI-powered cybersecurity platform secures operational technology (OT) and Internet of Things (IoT) infrastructures for enterprises and government entities across energy, manufacturing, transportation, resources, and critical infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As we expand our product portfolio and global presence, our Engineering department is seeking a Full-stack Data Engineer with a focus on AI and NLP. You’ll design, implement, and maintain highly available data pipelines that support our core products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use available technologies to develop medium to large features while proactively learning new ones and reducing technical debt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support colleagues to achieve overall team success and foster a collaborative environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embody Nozomi Networks&#39; Cultural Pillars and our mission to protect what matters most with transparency and trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate within an agile team that emphasizes automation and the creation of high-quality, well-designed software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of user-facing features from inception to release and beyond.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be successful in this opportunity you will have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and excellent analytical skill.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving capabilities with a solid understanding of algorithms, data structures, and concurrent programming.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in a dynamic programming language such as Python or Ruby.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Machine Learning and NLP is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Docker and prior frontend development experience, including knowledge of JavaScript and React, is highly desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.S. or M.S. in Computer Science, Mathematics, Statistics or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are and what we stand for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nozomi Networks is the leader in OT and IoT Cybersecurity. We protect the world&#39;s critical infrastructure, industrial and government organizations from cyber threats by providing exceptional network visibility, threat detection and operational insight. We’re always innovating and we hire the best at what they do to ensure our customers always have access to fast product enhancements, exceptional engineering support and rapid deployment across continents.&amp;nbsp;If you like a challenge, and value integrity and customer success, we invite you to help Nozomi Networks build the future of OT and IoT cybersecurity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging are part of our core beliefs, at Nozomi Networks. Diversity of thought, background and culture broadens our knowledge of the world and helps us learn, grow, and gain new perspectives. What makes us all different is what makes us powerful.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Global Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All of our benefits are customized to the country you are based in, naturally we want to get the best out of our Nozomiers, so we provide the best benefits packages, such as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health &amp;amp; Wellness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Financial&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work-Life Balance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unparalleled Flexible Time-Off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Need to know information&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Successful candidates will be subjected to background verification checks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Be cautious of unsolicited messages, fake email addresses, requests for money and unclear job descriptions. Report suspicious activity to authorities. Our open job opportunities and descriptions are posted on Nozomi Networks&#39; career page. If in any doubt please apply for opportunities on our careers website &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nozominetworks.com/company/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you would like to know more about our Privacy Policy, please click &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nozominetworks.com/legal/job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. Any questions about how we process personal information, or if you would like help exercising your privacy rights please contact us using the email provided within the Privacy Policy.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join Our Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a dynamic and customer-focused &lt;strong&gt;Solutions Consultant&lt;/strong&gt; to join our Commercial team in Zurich. This role is ideal for a professional who enjoys combining business insight with technical expertise to help clients solve complex challenges. As a key partner to our Sales, Product, and Operations teams, you will play a critical role in designing tailored solutions, accelerating sales cycles, and ensuring successful customer outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct discovery sessions with prospective clients to understand business processes, challenges, and technical requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex client needs into effective solution designs and technical specifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and present tailored solutions leveraging our product capabilities and integration options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver compelling product demonstrations, presentations, and proof-of-concept workshops for clients and stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the sales team as a technical and functional expert throughout the sales cycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and contribute to RFI and RFP responses, ensuring accuracy and alignment with customer expectations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide effort estimations and implementation guidance for proposed solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Product Development, Operations, and Implementation teams to ensure solution feasibility and successful delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather customer feedback and market insights to support product innovation and strategic decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop sales enablement materials, technical documentation, and case studies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum Bachelor&#39;s degree in Business, Logistics/Supply Chain Management, Computer Science, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience as a Solutions Consultant, Business Implementations, Presales Engineer, Solution Architect, or a similar customer-facing role within enterprise software, SaaS based environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of supply chain management, logistics, or related industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent ability to translate business requirements into technical solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CRM platforms and project management tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with integration technologies such as APIs and ETL processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent written and spoken English, other language skills are beneficial&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication, presentation, and stakeholder management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success in this role will be measured through:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High-quality and customer-focused solution designs and proposals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective support of the sales process resulting in accelerated deal closure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong customer satisfaction with demonstrations, presentations, and proposed solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accuracy and completeness of RFI/RFP responses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successful collaboration across Commercial, Product, Implementation, and Operations teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous contribution to product improvement through market and client insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increased conversion of qualified opportunities into successful customer engagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You Should Join Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work with innovative technology solutions in a dynamic commodity trading environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to international clients and complex business challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and entrepreneurial company culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct impact on business growth and customer success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close interaction with senior stakeholders and industry experts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional development and career growth opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An exciting role at the intersection of technology, consulting, and commercial strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you are passionate about solving business challenges, working with clients, and delivering innovative solutions that create real value, we&#39;d love to hear from you. Apply today and join our team as a Solutions Consultant&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join Our Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a customer-focused and detail-oriented &lt;strong&gt;Ocean Freight Customer Service Specialist &lt;/strong&gt;to join our growing team. This role is ideal for an experienced logistics or customer service professional who enjoys building strong customer relationships, resolving complex issues, and ensuring the smooth execution of ocean freight bookings and allocation management.&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;As the primary point of contact for our customers, you will play a key role in managing allocations, handling booking-related inquiries, supporting billing processes, and maintaining exceptional service standards across our global freight operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the main point of contact for customer inquiries regarding bookings, allocations, contract terms, and shipment updates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage day-to-day freight allocation requests and coordinate capacity requirements with the procurement team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide timely and accurate information on shipment status, allocation availability, and schedule changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate customer records and case documentation within CRM systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle customer disputes related to freight rates, surcharges, contracts, and service issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and prepare customer invoices, ensuring billing accuracy and commercial compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with carriers, operations, procurement, and finance teams to resolve customer and billing issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor allocation utilization and proactively communicate capacity constraints or opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and close customer cases within agreed service-level targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to customer service reporting and process improvement initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the maintenance and enhancement of customer service procedures and best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate complex customer matters appropriately while ensuring excellent customer experience throughout the resolution process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 3 years of experience in ocean freight, freight forwarding, logistics, or customer service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Business Administration, Logistics, International Trade, or a related field preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of ocean freight operations, shipping documentation, carrier tariffs, and Incoterms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Native-level German and fluent English communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with CRM platforms such as Salesforce, Zendesk, or similar systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and interpret freight contracts, rate sheets, and customer agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial understanding of ocean freight billing and invoice validation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, especially Outlook, Excel, and Word&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple customer cases and priorities simultaneously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer service or logistics certifications (e.g., FIATA, IATA) are considered an advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Personal Attributes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer-focused with a strong service mentality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving and analytical skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional and composed in challenging customer situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized and able to work effectively under pressure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative team player with excellent communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive, reliable, and solutions-oriented&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptable within a dynamic and fast-paced logistics environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success in this role will be measured through:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High customer satisfaction levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fast response times to customer inquiries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Timely resolution of customer disputes and service issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong case closure performance within SLA targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accurate customer communication and documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High invoice accuracy and low rework rates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective management of freight allocations and booking processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributions to customer service improvements and operational excellence initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You Should Join Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work within a global ocean freight procurement organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to international shipping markets, carrier management, and freight allocation strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative, entrepreneurial, and fast-growing business environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct impact on customer experience and operational performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work closely with procurement, operations, and finance teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional development and career growth opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenging and rewarding role with significant responsibility and customer interaction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modern workplace with an international team culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you are passionate about customer service, logistics, and building strong customer relationships in the ocean freight industry, we&#39;d love to hear from you. Apply today!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Mavericks Wanted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;When was the last time you achieved the impossible? If that thought feels overwhelming, you might want to pause here, but if it sparks excitement...read on&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;In 2015, we pioneered a “moneyball for biotech” approach, pooling projects and promising early-stage research from academia together under one financial umbrella to reduce risk and unleash innovation. This model allows science and small teams of experts to lead the way. We build bridges to groundbreaking advancements in rare&amp;nbsp;disease, and&amp;nbsp;develop life-changing medicines for patients with unmet needs as fast as humanly possible. &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Together we define white space, push boundaries, and empower people to solve problems. If you&#39;re someone who defies convention, join us and work alongside some of the most respected minds in the industry. Together, we&#39;ll&amp;nbsp;ask&amp;nbsp;&quot;why not?&quot; and help reengineer the future of biopharma. At BridgeBio, we value curiosity and experimentation—including the ethical &amp;amp; thoughtful use of AI to improve clarity, speed, and quality of work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;About BridgeBio Pharma, Inc.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BridgeBio is a biopharmaceutical company dedicated to discovering, developing, and delivering transformative medicines for patients living with genetic diseases and genetically defined cancers. Since our founding in 2015, we have built a diverse portfolio of more than 20 drug development programs, ranging from early discovery to late-stage clinical trials, across multiple therapeutic areas including precision oncology, cardiology, endocrinology, neurology, and renal disease. We have already achieved regulatory approval for three therapies and continue to advance promising science from academia into meaningful treatments for patients worldwide.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Who We Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BridgeBio is a global biotechnology company with our Global Headquarters located in San Francisco, USA, and our International HQ located in Zug, Switzerland. Since establishing our European presence in 2021, we’ve been building empowered, high-performing teams across countries — with experienced colleagues who move quickly, take ownership, and are fueling the company’s international growth.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At BridgeBio, you’ll find an energetic and collaborative culture where pragmatism meets bold decision-making. We embrace uncertainty with confidence, guided by our commitment to making a meaningful impact for patients. Our people are trusted and empowered, united by urgency, purpose, and the drive to advance science for patients around the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To learn more about our story and company culture, visit us at &lt;a href=&quot;https://bridgebio.com&quot;&gt;https://bridgebio.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report to the VP, Head of Market Access, International and work closely with international Market Access, regional brand team, and heads or markets access in BridgeBio clusters as well as with field-based colleagues across multiple geographies, to drive strategic initiatives that support BridgeBio’s mission of delivering transformative medicines to patients globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your primary purpose will be to secure timely, sustainable patient access to the company’s products by shaping the value narrative, and leading pricing and reimbursement strategies and execution across multiple international markets. This includes oversight of related dossiers, negotiations, and cost coverage approaches. In this role you ensure alignment of Market Access ambitions with clinical value and global pricing interdependencies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will also be a core member of the International Market Access team, contributing to global decision-making and ensuring alignment across regions while representing diverse market perspectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires strong collaboration with cross-functional colleagues and external stakeholders across multiple countries to ensure high-quality execution and impact. The ideal candidate combines deep expertise in Market Access processes across several international markets and experience introducing innovative therapies in a global biotech environment. You are eager to make a meaningful contribution in pre-launch and launch phases, particularly within rare diseases and orphan conditions, and bring strong communication skills, adaptability, and the ability to thrive in a fast-paced, hands-on environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the payer perspective within cross-functional, cross-regional commercialization teams thereby optimizing pricing and market access of the asset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Closely collaborate with HEOR and clusters&#39; leadership teams, Marketing and Clinical Development counterparts to ensure value and access optimization for the asset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead early payer engagement with key HTA/payer bodies (e.g. NICE UK, G-BA Germany) to inform evidence generation strategy, value proposition and reimbursement dossiers development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interact with internal and external experts in pricing, health economics, patient advocacy, health technology assessment authorities, government policy makers and payers as required to execute Pricing &amp;amp; Reimbursement objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide hands-on support and train local access teams on negotiation strategy and ensure HTA and reimbursement submissions are aligned to the Global and International strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Where You’ll Work&amp;nbsp; &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an office role based and requires in-office collaboration 2-3x per week in our Zug Office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Who You Are&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience leading HTA submissions and pricing negotiations across multiple international markets, ideally including Europe and other global regions, particularly in rare diseases and orphan conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of international healthcare systems, pricing and reimbursement frameworks, and regulatory environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience generating and leveraging data for HTA submissions and pricing negotiations, with a strong external network of agencies and stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable presenting at senior levels and engaging with external thought leaders globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience managing complex, cross-functional and multicultural teams (including external partners).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of product commercialization processes with a hands-on, solution-oriented mindset for building scalable processes and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Rewarding Those Who Make the Mission Possible&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have high expectations for our team members. We make sure those working hard for patients are rewarded and cared for in return.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market leading compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid work model - we value your flexibility in how you work, but encourage time in the office to strengthen our culture, collaboration, and sense of community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We provide career development through regular feedback, continuous education and professional development programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We celebrate strong performance with financial rewards, peer-to-peer recognition, and growth opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
